  mockups are token-heavy to produce, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  All three use the same controls and differ only in placement:

  - [1mA. Filter panel above the table, always open.[0m Everything is visible, but the table moves down.
  - [1mB. The two shortcut buttons always visible, with event type and date range in a "More filters" disclosure.[0m The
    common cases take one click, and the table stays near the top. I'd build the disclosure with native [38;5;153m<details>[39m.
  - [1mC. A sidebar to the left of the table.[0m It squeezes a six-column table and has to stack on narrow screens.

  [1mI recommend B.[0m Failed sign-ins and security changes are one click away, and checking a single week costs only one
  extra click.

